course: dictionary
lesson: 5057
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Insecure is one of these words. Read the words around it and ask: is this about feelings, safety, something fixed in place, or a job or home?
explain: «Feel insecure» is about feelings. When you feel insecure, you are not confident and you worry that you are not good enough or not liked. Try your meaning in the sentence: "I feel not confident and worried I am not good enough" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Insecure password» is about safety. A password that is not safe or protected could let someone in, such as a hacker. «Insecure job» means a job that might be lost. The clue is the word after insecure, so always look at the words that come next as well as before.
explain: When you meet insecure with a new partner word, use the clues to pick the meaning. A ladder that is not fixed firmly is insecure, and it might fall. A dictionary settles it when the clues are unclear.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Insecure is an adjective, and its noun is insecurity.
fact: Insecure can mean not confident, not safe, not fixed firmly, or likely to be lost.
fact: «Food insecure» (official) means hungry and not able to afford enough food.
fact: Informal friends may say «hard up» or «a bit short» instead, and old-fashioned speakers say «in reduced circumstances».
exercise: «She felt insecure about her new school, so she stayed close to her friend.» What does insecure mean here? | *Not confident, and worried she is not good enough | Very cold | Not fixed firmly, so it could move | Not safe, so someone could break in
exercise: «The shelf was insecure, so the books could fall.» What does insecure mean here? | Covered in dust | Not confident and worried | Not safe from thieves | *Not fixed firmly, so it might fall or move
exercise: «Food insecure» is an official phrase. What does it mean? | Lost in the shops | *Hungry and not able to afford enough food | Full of food and very happy | Able to cook any meal
test: «Dad lost his insecure job last month.» What does insecure mean here? | His job was very well paid | His job was on a high floor | *His job might be lost
test: «An insecure password can let hackers in.» Why is this a problem? | *Hackers could get into the account | Hackers will forget the password | It is too long to type | It is written in a foreign language
exam: Which word is the noun form of insecure? | securing | secure | insecurely | *insecurity
